{
  "abstract": "Every non-Hadamard real sign matrix has a direction of strictly negative curvature when its entries are allowed to vary through complex phases. We prove an energy-only criterion for unique one-entry repair and construct infinitely many matrices trapped under every one-entry and two-entry sign change. Further results classify rank-two Gram defects and provide constructive phase escape and exact rounding certificates. We also characterize four-phase accessibility under row and column phases, prove a signed complex-structure criterion for the corresponding real Hadamard construction from quaternary matrices, and give quantitative Fourier-Dita obstructions showing when these phase-based families cannot reach fourth-root entries. See README.md for the main theorem statements, RESULTS.md for further results, paper/main.pdf for proofs and citations, and TECHNICAL.md for formalization coverage and build details.",
